00:04:12.160 --> 00:04:15.280
Over those decades, politicians from both parties

00:04:15.280 --> 00:04:18.640
and at all levels passed harsher and harsher laws

00:04:18.640 --> 00:04:20.400
feeding the prison system.

00:04:20.400 --> 00:04:23.600
The war on drugs started in 1971.

00:04:23.600 --> 00:04:27.200
Cruel mandatory minimum laws came in the 1980s

00:04:27.200 --> 00:04:29.520
3 strikes laws arrived in the 90's.

00:04:29.520 --> 00:04:33.120
You could be put away for life without parole

00:04:33.120 --> 00:04:36.480
for stealing a pair of socks&nbsp;
if it was your third offense.

00:04:37.120 --> 00:04:42.240
"Tough on crime" prosecutors and judges&nbsp;
gained office across the country.

00:04:42.240 --> 00:04:45.600
Huge sums of money were spent&nbsp;
on building new prisons,

00:04:45.600 --> 00:04:47.600
which housed millions of people.

00:04:48.160 --> 00:04:51.440
As a result, incarceration rose DRAMATICALLY.

00:04:51.440 --> 00:04:55.280
In 1968, America's prison population was

00:04:55.280 --> 00:04:57.600
was 102 per 100,000 people,

00:04:58.160 --> 00:05:00.240
in line with other developed countries.

00:05:00.240 --> 00:05:05.280
By 2005, it had risen&nbsp;
sevenfold, to 737 per 100,000

00:05:06.000 --> 00:05:07.920
The highest in the world.

00:05:07.920 --> 00:05:09.280
Even as crimes fell,

00:05:09.280 --> 00:05:13.120
with murders in New York dropping 90% in the 90s,

00:05:13.120 --> 00:05:16.000
mass incarceration kept on growing.

00:05:16.000 --> 00:05:20.560
Why didn't prison populations&nbsp;
fall once crime started declining?

00:05:20.560 --> 00:05:24.240
it's because prisons are by&nbsp;
no means only "about crime,"

00:05:24.240 --> 00:05:28.160
they're also about keeping the&nbsp;
least advantaged people "in line."

00:05:28.160 --> 00:05:32.640
Prison has become the place to&nbsp;
warehouse people with mental illnesses,

00:05:32.640 --> 00:05:34.560
people experiencing homelessness,

00:05:34.560 --> 00:05:39.040
and people with addictions that&nbsp;
the system is not designed to help

00:05:39.040 --> 00:05:42.000
Instead of solving these problems, we use prison

00:05:42.000 --> 00:05:45.600
to disappear the people who have these problems.

00:05:45.600 --> 00:05:50.000
With this surging population,&nbsp;
prisons are crowded and violent.

00:05:50.000 --> 00:05:53.040
People in prison are robbed of their humanity,

00:05:53.040 --> 00:05:55.360
often brutalized by guards,

00:05:55.360 --> 00:05:58.160
and without real rehabilitation, or

00:05:58.160 --> 00:06:01.040
